{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba README.md | sed -n '124,136p'\"","aggregated_output":"   124\t\n   125\t![Darkfactory architecture diagram](docs/architecture.png)\n   126\t\n   127\t### Three roles\n   128\t\n   129\tThe system has three roles, each handled by a separate AI agent:\n   130\t\n   131\t**Orchestrator** -- the main Claude Code session you interact with. It plans the work, sends out one worker at a time, reads their results, runs validators, and decides what to do next. It uses Claude Code's \"plan mode,\" which keeps its instructions alive even when the conversation gets long enough that older messages are dropped to save space.\n   132\t\n   133\t**Workers** -- each worker builds a single task. By default, workers are powered by Codex (OpenAI's coding agent), but you can use Claude instead. Codex workers are dispatched through `darkfactory-dispatch`, a Rust process supervisor that provides process group isolation, two-phase timeout (SIGTERM then SIGKILL), heartbeat events every 15 seconds, and structured JSON results. Claude workers use Claude Code's built-in Agent tool. A worker gets a brief with everything it needs: what to build, how the project is structured, coding rules to follow, which exact Type Catalog domain type names to use, which files to look at, and a summary of what previous tasks already built (file paths, function names, and types -- facts only, never reasoning from other workers). It makes its changes in a single commit and writes a report describing what it did. Workers never see the contract -- they only know what the brief tells them.\n   134\t\n   135\t**Validators** -- after each worker finishes, validators check the work against the contract. Two validators run back-to-back for every task: the scrutiny validator (a thorough quality check) and the user-test validator (which tests the feature the way a real user would). Validators never see the proposal or design documents -- they only see the code and the contract.\n   136\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQE4EJ2EGRYEET558ZVNHM9F","ts":"2026-04-30T02:46:44Z","tool":"command_execution"}
