{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/SKILL.md | sed -n '680,716p'\"","aggregated_output":"   680\t1. Mark the task complete in `tasks.md`: change `- [ ]` to `- [x]` for this task.\n   681\t\n   682\t2. **Generate codebase delta for subsequent briefs.** Run `git diff $PRE_TASK_SHA..HEAD` (where `PRE_TASK_SHA` is the value recorded in Step 2 before this task was dispatched) to extract what this task added. Summarize into a codebase delta entry containing: files created/modified (paths), public function/endpoint signatures, key types, and patterns used. Store this delta in the plan under a `## Codebase Deltas` section. The next task's brief (Step 1) reads accumulated deltas from the plan and writes them into the \"What Previous Tasks Built\" section.\n   683\t\n   684\t   **Guard rail:** Generate the delta from `git diff` output only. Never read handoff reports to build this summary. The delta contains facts about what exists in the code, not why or how the worker built it.\n   685\t\n   686\t3. Append to `progress.md`:\n   687\t\n   688\t```markdown\n   689\t- <timestamp> -- Task N complete.\n   690\t  - Commit: <SHA>\n   691\t  - Scrutiny: PASS\n   692\t  - User-test: PASS | SKIP\n   693\t  - Demo: RECORDED | SKIPPED | FAILED\n   694\t  - Fix attempts: <number, 0 if first try passed>\n   695\t```\n   696\t\n   697\t4. Update the plan: set Current Task to the next unchecked task, or \"none\" if all done.\n   698\t\n   699\t4a. **Foundation audit (after task 1 only).** If this is task 1 and it passed both validators, run a foundation check before proceeding to task 2:\n   700\t\n   701\t   - Read task 1's Produces field from its topology metadata in tasks.md\n   702\t   - Extract module names from the Produces field. Look up those modules in design.md's Module Inventory. Verify that corresponding directories or files exist in the committed code with matching names.\n   703\t   - Extract type names from the Produces field. Look up those types in design.md's Type Catalog. Verify that corresponding type definitions exist in the committed code with matching names.\n   704\t\n   705\t   If drift is detected (module structure or type names do not match the design for items task 1 declared it would produce):\n   706\t   - Generate a corrective task 1a\n   707\t   - Insert it in tasks.md between task 1 and task 2\n   708\t   - Add assertions for it to contract.md\n   709\t   - Present both to the human for approval\n   710\t   - The corrective task goes through the normal build loop before task 2 starts\n   711\t\n   712\t   If no drift: log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Foundation audit PASSED. Module structure and type names confirmed for task 1 produces.`\n   713\t\n   714\t   This audit runs only after task 1. It does not run after any other task.\n   715\t\n   716\t5. **If more tasks remain:** Go back to Step 1 for the next task.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
