{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/SKILL.md | sed -n '565,615p'\"","aggregated_output":"   565\tThe Bash tool returns a shell task ID immediately and notifies you when it completes. On completion, call BashOutput on that shell task ID to retrieve stdout. The only thing on stdout is the single final line -- either `TASK_COMPLETE` or `TASK_FAILED` -- because all codex output was redirected to `$LOG_PATH`.\n   566\t\n   567\t- `TASK_COMPLETE` -> proceed to Step 3\n   568\t- `TASK_FAILED` -> proceed to Step 3 (failure path). Read `$LOG_PATH` for failure context before asking the human.\n   569\t\n   570\t**Human visibility:** To watch dispatch progress live, run `tail -f <absolute path to mission/logs/task-N-codex.log>` in another terminal. The log contains both codex output and dispatcher events (heartbeats every 15 seconds, timeout warnings, tool activity). If the configured timeout is reached, the dispatcher kills the codex process automatically (SIGTERM at soft timeout, SIGKILL after grace period).\n   571\t\n   572\t#### If engine is `claude`:\n   573\t\n   574\tUse the Agent tool to spawn a subagent. Pass the full brief content as the prompt. Instruct the subagent to write its handoff to the same path (`mission/handoffs/task-N.md`).\n   575\t\n   576\t### Step 3: Handle Result\n   577\t\n   578\tRead the handoff file at `mission/handoffs/task-N.md`.\n   579\t\n   580\t- **TASK_COMPLETE** (handoff exists and contains a commit SHA): Extract the commit SHA. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: worker completed. Commit: <SHA>`. Proceed to Step 4.\n   581\t- **TASK_FAILED** (handoff missing or no commit SHA):\n   582\t  1. If engine is `codex` and this is the first failure for this task: log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: codex worker failed. Falling back to claude worker.` Append a line to `mission/fallbacks.log`: `task-N|<task-name>|<reason for failure>`. Then dispatch a claude worker (Opus 4.6, extended thinking high) using the existing \"If engine is `claude`\" dispatch path with the same brief. Wait for the result.\n   583\t     - If the claude fallback produces `TASK_COMPLETE`: log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: claude fallback succeeded. Commit: <SHA>.` Proceed to Step 4.\n   584\t     - If the claude fallback also fails: fall through to the human escalation below.\n   585\t  2. Human escalation (reached when: engine is `claude`, engine is `codex` and both attempts failed, or any second failure): log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: worker FAILED. <reason>.` Ask the human: retry, skip, or abort. If skip: mark the task as `- [~]` in tasks.md and log `<timestamp> -- Task N: SKIPPED by human.` to progress.md. The build loop ignores `- [~]` tasks.\n   586\t  3. On the next task, revert to the configured engine. This fallback is per-task only. Before starting the next task, re-read `engine` from `openspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/config.yaml` so the engine resets to the configured value after any Codex -> Claude fallback.\n   587\t\n   588\t### Step 4: Scrutiny Validation\n   589\t\n   590\tSpawn a Claude subagent (via the Agent tool) with this prompt:\n   591\t\n   592\t#### Scrutiny Validator Prompt\n   593\t\n   594\tRead [prompts/scrutiny-validator.md](prompts/scrutiny-validator.md) and use it as the subagent prompt. Fill in the commit SHA and contract assertions for this task. The prompt runs 11 checks: test presence, build, tests, lint, code review, module depth, code standards, simplify, security (if applicable), contract assertions, behavioral conformance.\n   595\t\n   596\tRead the validator's report from `mission/validations/task-N-scrutiny.md`.\n   597\t\n   598\t### Step 5: Handle Scrutiny Validation Result\n   599\t\n   600\t- **PASS**: Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: scrutiny validation PASSED.` Proceed to Step 6.\n   601\t- **FAIL**: Proceed to Step 5a (fix loop).\n   602\t\n   603\t### Step 5a: Fix Loop\n   604\t\n   605\tTrack the attempt number (starts at 1 for the initial worker, increments on each fix).\n   606\t\n   607\t1. **Write failure details** to `mission/issues/task-N-v<attempt>.md`:\n   608\t\n   609\t```markdown\n   610\t# Issue: Task N - <name> (Attempt <attempt>)\n   611\t\n   612\t## Failed Checks\n   613\t<list of failed checks from validator report>\n   614\t\n   615\t## Observed Symptoms\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
