{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/SKILL.md | sed -n '500,565p'\"","aggregated_output":"   500\t\n   501\t## Phase 8: Build Loop\n   502\t\n   503\t> **Rules:** 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9\n   504\t> **Goal:** Build all tasks with per-task validation.\n   505\t> **Inputs:** tasks.md, contract.md, design.md, proposal.md, config.yaml, UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n   506\t> **Outputs:** Committed code per task, validation reports in mission/validations/. Codebase deltas are internal (populate subsequent task briefs within this phase).\n   507\t\n   508\tFor each unchecked task (`- [ ]`) in tasks.md, run Steps 1-7. Process tasks in order, one at a time (serial execution). Skip tasks marked `- [~]` (skipped) and `- [x]` (complete).\n   509\t\n   510\t### Step 1: Assemble Brief\n   511\t\n   512\tWrite a brief to `mission/briefs/task-N.md`.\n   513\t\n   514\t#### Brief Template\n   515\t\n   516\tRead [templates/worker-brief.md](templates/worker-brief.md).\n   517\t\n   518\t**The brief NEVER contains contract.md content.** \n   519\t\n   520\t### Step 2: Dispatch Worker\n   521\t\n   522\tRead the engine from `mission/config.yaml`.\n   523\t\n   524\t#### If engine is `codex`:\n   525\t\n   526\tBefore dispatching, run `git rev-parse HEAD` and store the result as `PRE_TASK_SHA`. This value is used in Step 7 to generate the codebase delta — store it somewhere you can reference after the background worker returns (e.g. in the plan file or a local variable).\n   527\t\n   528\tUse the Bash tool with `run_in_background: true` to run the worker. Use this exact bash script:\n   529\t\n   530\t```bash\n   531\tBRIEF_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/briefs/task-N.md>\"\n   532\tHANDOFF_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/handoffs/task-N.md>\"\n   533\tLOG_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/logs/task-N-codex.log>\"\n   534\tPRE_TASK_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n   535\t# Clean stale temp files and directories from previous workers to avoid filling /tmp\n   536\tfind /tmp -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -user \"$(whoami)\" -mmin +30 -not -name \"claude-*\" \\( -type f -delete -o -type d -exec rm -rf {} + \\) 2>/dev/null\n   537\t\n   538\t# Dispatch via darkfactory-dispatch: process supervisor with timeout, heartbeat, and structured JSON result\n   539\tDISPATCH_RESULT=$(darkfactory-dispatch \\\n   540\t  --model gpt-5.5 \\\n   541\t  --effort high \\\n   542\t  --timeout 1800 \\\n   543\t  --sandbox workspace-write \\\n   544\t  --config 'sandbox_workspace_write.writable_roots=[\".git\"]' \\\n   545\t  --prompt-file \"$BRIEF_PATH\" \\\n   546\t  --output \"$HANDOFF_PATH\" \\\n   547\t  --cwd \"$(pwd)\" \\\n   548\t  --log \"$LOG_PATH\" \\\n   549\t  --json 2>>\"$LOG_PATH\")\n   550\t\n   551\tif [ -z \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" ]; then\n   552\t  echo \"TASK_FAILED: dispatcher crashed with no output. Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   553\telse\n   554\t  DISPATCH_STATUS=$(echo \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.status')\n   555\t  DISPATCH_ERROR=$(echo \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.error.message // empty')\n   556\t\n   557\t  if [ \"$DISPATCH_STATUS\" = \"completed\" ] && [ -f \"$HANDOFF_PATH\" ]; then\n   558\t    echo \"TASK_COMPLETE: handoff written\"\n   559\t  else\n   560\t    echo \"TASK_FAILED: dispatch status $DISPATCH_STATUS${DISPATCH_ERROR:+; error: $DISPATCH_ERROR}; handoff $([ -f \"$HANDOFF_PATH\" ] && echo present || echo missing). Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   561\t  fi\n   562\tfi\n   563\t```\n   564\t\n   565\tThe Bash tool returns a shell task ID immediately and notifies you when it completes. On completion, call BashOutput on that shell task ID to retrieve stdout. The only thing on stdout is the single final line -- either `TASK_COMPLETE` or `TASK_FAILED` -- because all codex output was redirected to `$LOG_PATH`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
