ate README.md to reflect the new Domain Types section in worker briefs, the domain type boundary clarification in the design template, and the Type Catalog name verification in the module shape re-check. Note that UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md was already updated before the build loop and should not be re-edited.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Closing Tasks\n    30\t\n    31\t- [x] Task 4: Smoke test\n    32\t  Depends on: Task 1, Task 2, Task 3\n    33\t  Consumes: all prior task outputs\n    34\t  Produces: validation that templates are syntactically valid markdown\n    35\t  Layers: validation\n    36\t\n    37\t  Verify all modified markdown files are syntactically valid. Run a markdown lint or parse check on worker-brief.md, design-template.md, SKILL.md, UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md, and README.md. No project-internal mocks. Since this mission produces no runnable user flow, note that in the handoff.\n    38\t\n    39\t- [x] Task 5: Cleanup\n    40\t  Depends on: Task 4\n    41\t  Consumes: all prior task outputs\n    42\t  Produces: clean codebase with no leftover scaffolding\n    43\t  Layers: cleanup\n    44\t\n    45\t  Remove unused dependencies, dead code, leftover scaffolding, temporary artifacts, and any backwards-compatibility shims. Check for any debris from the build process.\n    46\t\n    47\t- [x] Task 6: Module shape re-check\n    48\t  Depends on: Task 5\n    49\t  Consumes: design.md Module Inventory\n    50\t  Produces: mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md\n    51\t  Layers: validation\n    52\t\n    53\t  Re-read design.md's module descriptions. For each module, compare the description to what the files actually contain. Write findings to mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md. Also verify that every domain type in the Type Catalog exists in the committed code with a matching name (which is trivially satisfied since this mission introduces no domain types).\n    54\t\n    55\t- [x] Task 7: CLAUDE.md + ARCH.md generation\n    56\t  Depends on: Task 6\n    57\t  Consumes: design.md, built codebase\n    58\t  Produces: CLAUDE.md and/or ARCH.md if they don't already exist\n    59\t  Layers: documentation\n    60\t\n    61\t  If CLAUDE.md does not exist in the project root, create one. If it already exists, do not modify it. Similarly for ARCH.md.\n    62\t\n    63\t- [x] Task 8: Documentation\n    64\t  Depends on: Task 7\n    65\t  Consumes: all changes from feature tasks\n    66\t  Produces: updated documentation\n    67\t  Layers: documentation\n    68\t\n    69\t  Write or update documentation for what was built. Use terms from UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md consistently. Any commands shown in docs must be executed against the built artifacts and the actual output pasted.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
