{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/domain-vocabulary-type-names/mission/validations/adversarial-a-v2.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial Review A (v2)\n\n## Task 1 -- [task-1] Add Domain Types section to worker brief template\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n\n## Task 2 -- [task-2] Add domain type boundary and Type Catalog name verification\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n\n## Task 3 -- [task-3] Update README to reflect domain vocabulary changes\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n\n## Task 4 -- [task-5] Cleanup: commit pre-build UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md changes\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n| 1 | Warning | `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md:95` | The Type Catalog definition says types not in the glossary are \"named by the worker.\" That reverses the authority chain described elsewhere: design.md's Type Catalog is produced during planning before workers run, and worker briefs tell workers to use exact Type Catalog names. A future worker could read this as permission to invent names instead of preserving the planned names. |\n\n## Task 5 -- [task-7] Add ARCH.md\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n| 1 | Warning | `ARCH.md:59` | The architecture doc says the foundation audit checks module structure and type names \"against the design\" after task 1. `skills/mission/SKILL.md:699-714` limits that audit to modules and types declared in task 1's Produces field, not the full design. This overstates early coverage and can make readers think the whole Type Catalog is verified before task 2. |\n| 2 | Nit | `ARCH.md:45` | The skill installation description only mentions symlinks into `~/.claude/skills/`, but `install.sh` also links skills into `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/`. For an architecture reference, leaving out the Codex and Agents discovery paths is incomplete and can confuse debugging. |\n\n## Task 6 -- [task-8] Documentation: add ARCH.md to Key references, fix stale term count\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n\n## Task 7 -- Fix adversarial review findings: verb forms, line count, glossary term\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n\n## Cross-task\n| # | Severity | File | Finding |\n|---|----------|------|---------|\n| 1 | Nit | `README.md:80`, `skills/mission/SKILL.md:258-260` | README lists the mandatory closing tasks as module shape re-check, documentation, then CLAUDE.md + ARCH.md generation. SKILL.md defines the actual order as module shape re-check, CLAUDE.md + ARCH.md generation, then documentation, and this mission's `tasks.md` follows SKILL.md. The mismatch is minor, but it forces readers to reconcile two different sequences. |\n\n## Summary\nThe commit stack is mostly coherent and the markdown syntax is intact, but the final docs still have a few authority-chain problems. The biggest issue is `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` saying workers name Type Catalog entries that are not already in the glossary, which conflicts with the rest of the workflow where the design owns Type Catalog names and workers consume them. `ARCH.md` also overstates what the task-1 foundation audit verifies, and its install description omits two symlink targets that matter for Codex and Agents. The remaining cross-task issue is a small but real ordering mismatch between README and SKILL.md for mandatory closing tasks.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
